IMPORT prelude

-- Trustees Act 1967 (Singapore) -- the statutory duty of care (s 3A), investment (ss 4 to 6, 9, 10), advancement (s 34), the
-- number and replacement of trustees (ss 36, 37), delegation (ss 41B, 41N), remuneration (ss 41Q, 41R), relief for breach
-- (s 60) and impounding a beneficiary's interest (s 61).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/TA1967.txt.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 16 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to what a private trustee and a
-- beneficiary most often need. Not encoded: the powers of sale, receipts and insurance (Part 3 beyond s 34), maintenance (s 33),
-- protective trusts (s 35), vesting (s 41, Part 5 orders), nominees and custodians beyond liability, expenses, payment into
-- court, and charitable trusts (Part 6).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Trustees Act 1967 -- trustees`

§§ `3A -- the duty of care`

-- s 3A(1): reasonable care and skill, having regard to the trustee's special knowledge, or, for a trustee acting in the course
-- of a business or profession, the knowledge expected of that kind of professional. (2): applies "except if, or insofar as, it
-- appears from the trust instrument that the requirements ... are not meant to apply" -- the settlor can exclude it.
GIVEN `the instrument excludes the duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the statutory duty of care applies` IF
    NOT `the instrument excludes the duty`

§§ `4 to 6, 9, 10 -- investment`

-- s 4(1)(a): a trustee may make "any kind of investment that the trustee could have made if the trustee were absolutely entitled".
-- s 5: must have regard to suitability and "the need for diversification", and review from time to time.
-- s 6(1): must "obtain and consider proper advice" before investing, (3) unless the trustee "reasonably concludes that in all the
-- circumstances it is unnecessary or inappropriate".
-- s 9(1): lending on property is not a breach "by reason only of the proportion" of loan to value if made on proper advice and not
-- exceeding TWO-THIRDS of the advised value.
-- s 10(1): if a trustee advances too much on a mortgage that was proper for a smaller sum, the security is authorised for the
-- smaller sum and the trustee "is only liable to make good the sum advanced in excess", with interest.
GIVEN `took proper advice` IS A BOOLEAN, `reasonably concluded advice was unnecessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the advice requirement is met` IF
    `took proper advice` OR `reasonably concluded advice was unnecessary`

GIVEN `the loan` IS A NUMBER, `the advised value` IS A NUMBER, `on proper advice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the loan-to-value is protected` IF
    `on proper advice` AND `the loan` TIMES 3 AT MOST `the advised value` TIMES 2

GIVEN `the amount advanced` IS A NUMBER, `the proper amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the trustee's liability for over-advancing` MEANS
    IF `the amount advanced` GREATER THAN `the proper amount` THEN `the amount advanced` MINUS `the proper amount` ELSE 0

§§ `34 -- advancement`

-- s 34(1): trustees may pay capital for the "advancement or benefit" of a person entitled to capital, even contingently.
-- (3): the total advanced "must not exceed altogether in amount ONE-HALF of the presumptive or vested share", and is brought into
-- account. (4): not so as to prejudice a prior life or other interest, unless that person "is in existence and of full age and
-- consents in writing".
GIVEN `the beneficiary's share` IS A NUMBER, `already advanced` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that can still be advanced` MEANS
    IF `already advanced` TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `the beneficiary's share` THEN 0
    ELSE `the beneficiary's share` DIVIDED BY 2 MINUS `already advanced`

GIVEN `there is a prior life interest` IS A BOOLEAN, `the life tenant is an adult and consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the advancement may prejudice the prior interest` IF
    (NOT `there is a prior life interest`) OR `the life tenant is an adult and consented in writing`

§§ `36, 37 -- number and replacement of trustees`

-- s 36(1): for private trusts, "the number of trustees must not in any case exceed 4"; where more are named, "the 4 first named
-- (who are able and willing to act) must alone be the trustees". (2): no limit for charitable, religious or public trusts.
-- s 37(1): a trustee may be replaced if dead, OUT OF SINGAPORE FOR MORE THAN 12 MONTHS, wishing to be discharged, refusing,
-- unfit, incapable, or an infant.
GIVEN `trustees named` IS A NUMBER, `is charitable or public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number who are trustees` MEANS
    IF `is charitable or public` THEN `trustees named`
    ELSE IF `trustees named` GREATER THAN 4 THEN 4 ELSE `trustees named`

DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `death`
    `abroad for 18 months`
    `abroad for 6 months`
    `wishes to retire`
    `unfit to act`
    `is an infant`
    `disagrees with co-trustees`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trustee may be replaced on this ground` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `abroad for 6 months` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `disagrees with co-trustees` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `41B, 41N -- delegation`

-- s 41B(2): trustees of a private trust may delegate any function EXCEPT (a) deciding whether or how to distribute assets,
-- (b) deciding whether payments come from income or capital, (c) appointing trustees, (d) powers to delegate.
-- s 41N(1): a trustee is not liable for an agent's default unless the trustee breached the duty of care in appointing or
-- reviewing the agent.
DECLARE Function IS ONE OF
    `managing the investments`
    `collecting rent`
    `deciding which beneficiary gets a distribution`
    `deciding whether a fee comes from income or capital`
    `appointing a new trustee`

GIVEN `the function` IS A Function
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the function can be delegated` IF
    CONSIDER `the function`
    WHEN `managing the investments` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `collecting rent` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `took care in appointing and reviewing the agent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trustee is liable for the agent's default` IF
    NOT `took care in appointing and reviewing the agent`

§§ `41Q, 41R -- remuneration`

-- s 41R(1): a TRUST CORPORATION is entitled to reasonable remuneration. (2): a trustee acting in a professional capacity who is
-- "not a trust corporation OR A SOLE TRUSTEE" is entitled only if "each other trustee has agreed in writing". (4): neither applies
-- where the trust instrument (or any written law) makes "any provision about the entitlement to remuneration". A lay trustee has
-- no statutory remuneration.
-- s 41Q(2): where the instrument allows payment, a professional trustee may charge even for work a lay trustee could do.
--
-- A solicitor acting as SOLE trustee of a trust that says nothing about payment has no statutory right to be paid at all. A
-- trust corporation in the same position does.
DECLARE Trustee IS ONE OF
    `a trust corporation`
    `a professional co-trustee`
    `a professional sole trustee`
    `a lay trustee`

GIVEN `the trustee` IS A Trustee, `the instrument deals with remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN, `all other trustees agreed in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trustee has statutory remuneration` IF
        (NOT `the instrument deals with remuneration`)
    AND CONSIDER `the trustee`
        WHEN `a trust corporation` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a professional co-trustee` THEN `all other trustees agreed in writing`
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `60, 61 -- relief and impounding`

-- s 60: the court may relieve a trustee wholly or partly if the trustee "has acted honestly AND reasonably, AND ought fairly to be
-- excused".
-- s 61(1): where a breach was committed "at the instigation or request or with the WRITTEN consent of a beneficiary", the court
-- may impound that beneficiary's interest to indemnify the trustee. (The section still refers to "a married woman restrained from
-- anticipation".)
GIVEN `acted honestly` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted reasonably` IS A BOOLEAN, `ought fairly to be excused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may relieve the trustee` IF
    `acted honestly` AND `acted reasonably` AND `ought fairly to be excused`

DECLARE Involvement IS ONE OF
    `instigated the breach`
    `requested the breach`
    `consented in writing`
    `consented orally`
    `knew but said nothing`

GIVEN `the involvement` IS AN Involvement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the beneficiary's interest may be impounded` IF
    CONSIDER `the involvement`
    WHEN `consented orally` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `knew but said nothing` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
